WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:06.000
There were a few rumors after the break of&nbsp;
day came, whispers that were passed on from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.220
the lips of trader caravans as they traveled&nbsp;
from settlement to settlement. Not many people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:16.980
would have believed it way back when; it sounded&nbsp;
just like a legend out of an old Western. Too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:24.000
good to be true. A shadowy stranger wandering the&nbsp;
wasteland, righting wrongs wherever he finds them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Then, when the job’s done, and innocent people&nbsp;
are safe once more, he walks off into the horizon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.700
without asking for so much as a ‘thank you’.
Like we said, folks would’ve had a hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.320
time believing such a fanciful tale… of&nbsp;
course, that was before the Sun started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.600
shining an anomalous light over the world.&nbsp;
Nowadays, people might believe anything.&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.920
The earliest days of this strange new world&nbsp;
proved to be a learning experience for SCP-4494.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.760
Otherwise known as The Specter, he was the&nbsp;
physical embodiment of the very notion of fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:05.280
crime. Wherever injustice arose, he would appear&nbsp;
to vanquish those that preyed on the innocent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.080
While he usually manifested at night, he never&nbsp;
used to have any trouble appearing in the day time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.620
too – in the form of a shadowy figure, wearing&nbsp;
a wide-brimmed hat and a long, flowing coat that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:22.200
he could alter the length of for added dramatic&nbsp;
flourish. The Specter’s form absorbed almost all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.840
the light from the visible spectrum, but after&nbsp;
day broke, the rules seemed to have changed.&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.000
One day, The Specter had emerged to find the&nbsp;
sunlight had become unbearable. Where he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.520
once been a void of any and all light, he was now&nbsp;
finding it impossible to manifest during daylight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:45.060
The moment that the unrelenting light from the Sun&nbsp;
made contact with him, SCP-4494 would dissipate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:51.720
yet he kept reappearing at night. It was like he&nbsp;
was being pulled back into existence, and was only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:57.180
able to remanifest in the moonlight. Despite it&nbsp;
being a reflection of the anomalous sunlight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:03.900
that was seemingly enough to negate the effects&nbsp;
it had of preventing SCP-4494 from reappearing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:10.020
The same couldn’t be said for any humans caught in&nbsp;
the light though; a far worse fate awaited them.&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.120
Even with much of mankind deformed into&nbsp;
creatures that resembled melted wax, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.640
were still pockets of survivors around. And where&nbsp;
there were human beings, there’d be subsects that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:26.520
wanted to harm or exploit their fellow man. The&nbsp;
world might have had no governing bodies anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:34.740
no law and order. But The Specter had realized&nbsp;
that even in a lawless world, his work wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:40.440
done. As long as there were survivors of&nbsp;
the break of day, they’d still need saving:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:47.340
not just from the fleshy hordes of SCP-001-A&nbsp;
roaming the wastes, but saving from each other.&nbsp;

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:52.860
Striding through the remains of the old world in&nbsp;
the dead of night, his long cloak billowed out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:59.280
behind him. Its shadow almost seemed to blend with&nbsp;
the darkness that surrounded The Specter. But on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:05.580
the horizon, there was a sight he didn’t often see&nbsp;
these days: light. Not coming from the Sun above,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:11.280
nor the Moon, but instead, it lay ahead&nbsp;
of him, a fire glowing not too far away.&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:18.540
As he wandered closer, like an outlaw striding&nbsp;
into town, SCP-4494 was presented with the ruins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:23.880
of a small settlement. Around him, shacks&nbsp;
burned, their boarded-up windows broken to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:29.340
allow the cursed sunlight in. Everyone that was&nbsp;
still alive normally kept themselves wrapped up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:34.500
head to toe to block out the Sun, but there were&nbsp;
clothes and protective goggles strewn all around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:42.780
a larger pile of garments fuelling a bonfire.&nbsp;
SCP-4494 had witnessed the SCP-001-A creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:48.480
attacking humans, dragging them out into the&nbsp;
light to be transformed into more of the anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.400
abominations. But what had happened here&nbsp;
didn’t seem to be the work of those creatures…&nbsp;

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.900
The Specter’s suspicions were confirmed&nbsp;
when he approached the town square,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:03.120
to find a group of people who had all been&nbsp;
melted into a fleshy mass. The instance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:09.660
SCP-001-A paid the crimefighter little mind; it&nbsp;
couldn’t move very far. The few vaguely human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.860
shapes that protruded out of it looked like&nbsp;
they were tethered to poles in the middle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:19.560
the settlement. It didn’t take much longer for&nbsp;
SCP-4494 to figure out what had happened here.&nbsp;

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:25.440
Someone had ransacked the settlement, for some&nbsp;
unknown reason. Maybe they wanted something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.660
maybe they were opportunists just looking to&nbsp;
take advantage of this new post-apocalyptic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.820
world. Or perhaps they just wanted to be&nbsp;
cruel to these settlers. They had broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.740
the barricades over the windows that blocked out&nbsp;
the sunlight. They had trashed the ramshackle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:46.860
homesteads that these innocent settlers had&nbsp;
been residing in. As SCP-4494 looked further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:52.440
there looked to have been looting too; food&nbsp;
and water, medical supplies and ammunition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.920
not anything of use to be found. All that was left&nbsp;
was what these raiders hadn’t had any need for.&nbsp;

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:04.200
But as if all that hadn’t been enough, as if&nbsp;
robbing the settlers for what little livelihood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.900
they had left wasn’t enough cruelty, the bandits&nbsp;
had tethered the survivors to poles in the center&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:15.900
of town. They had taken away their protective&nbsp;
gear, and left them at the mercy of the elements.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.480
And as the Sun had crept higher into the sky, and&nbsp;
bathed the captive settlers in its unforgiving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:30.480
light, they had melted into an SCP-001-A creature.
Turning away from the town, The Specter did his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:35.160
best to quell his rage. He wandered in the&nbsp;
direction of the next settlement. Something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:40.140
was drawing him there; he could feel the pull&nbsp;
of the wrongdoers that had left this carnage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:45.360
in their wake. He’d find them, and they would&nbsp;
pay for what they had done. There was nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.800
he could do for their last victims, they&nbsp;
had already been turned by the sunlight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:55.560
But if anyone could save the next group of&nbsp;
survivors, it was him. As the wind howled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.900
the shadowy figure’s cloak flapped in the breeze.
The next settlement looked similar to the last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:06.480
although still intact. Shacks built from sheets&nbsp;
of corrugated iron and other scrap metal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:12.540
all welded together so that not even as little as&nbsp;
a tiny beam of sunlight could bleed through. As he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:17.580
stepped towards the boundary of the settlement, a&nbsp;
muzzle flashed, accompanied by the deafening echo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.800
of a gunshot that reverberated all around.&nbsp;
Someone had tried to shoot at The Specter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:27.660
narrowly missing, the bullet whizzing past his&nbsp;
head. Not that it would have harmed him anyway.&nbsp;

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:32.760
“Fear not,” he declared. “You can&nbsp;
hold your fire. I mean you no harm.”&nbsp;

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:37.020
“You aren’t with The Slivers?” a&nbsp;
voice called in the nightly dark.&nbsp;

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:41.460
“If you mean the evil doers that left the&nbsp;
last settlement over a smoldering ruin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:47.700
then no, I am not,” The Specter replied.
Hearing this, he spotted movement on one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:53.340
of the shack rooftops. A sharpshooter, carrying&nbsp;
a worn old rifle, stood up, covered in layers of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:57.840
protection from the transformative effects&nbsp;
of the Sun’s light reflected off the Moon.&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.580
“Well, you aren’t dressed like they are, I’ll&nbsp;
give you that,” the sharpshooter called. “Can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.120
barely make you out wearing all those dark&nbsp;
clothes, mister. But if you’re looking to trade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:12.000
I’m afraid your timing couldn’t be much worse.”
“Tell me,” replied The Specter bluntly. “The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.940
criminals that terrorized the other&nbsp;
settlement, they’ve been here too?”&nbsp;

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:19.260
“Yessir!” the man answered. “Said&nbsp;
they’d be back tonight too.”&nbsp;

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:24.000
“I have come to help, to do away with those&nbsp;
that would inflict injustice on the innocent,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:30.360
SCP-4494 explained in his typically dramatic&nbsp;
cadence. “You called them Slivers, yes?”&nbsp;

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:34.740
“Well, they call themselves that,” the&nbsp;
sharpshooter said. “On the count of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:39.060
choice in outfits. They look ridiculous, but&nbsp;
they’ve covered their protective clothing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.260
slivers of metal and glass. That way they’re&nbsp;
not only protected from the light, but their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:47.640
clothes reflect it back at other people too.”
“Dastardly villains taking advantage of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:52.680
has befallen the Sun,” The Specter cursed the&nbsp;
bandits. “Why are they yet to pillage your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:57.360
settlement? You said they intended to return?”
“That’s what they threatened earlier! The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.820
lot of them have been ransacking any&nbsp;
settlement that they can’t shakedown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:04.860
They showed up here in their stupid sparking&nbsp;
outfits and demanded we hand over half of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:09.720
our food, water, and antibiotics. They call&nbsp;
it their ‘Sunshine Tax’. According to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.620
if we didn’t meet their demands, they’d destroy&nbsp;
the town. We didn’t know to take them seriously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:19.440
until we saw the fire over there on the horizon.”
For a moment, The Specter fell silent. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:24.300
cloak had slowed, waving gently now the&nbsp;
winds had died down. But in contrast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.560
his anger had never been higher.
“Who are you anyway, mister?” the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:33.180
sharpshooter asked. “Never got your name.”
“My name is The Specter, a name these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:38.820
vagabonds will soon know well. For tonight,&nbsp;
they will pay the price for their crimes.”&nbsp;

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:43.800
“No offense, Mister, uh, Mister Specter,&nbsp;
but look around. World’s gone to hell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.340
ain’t no justice anymore. What price&nbsp;
are you expecting to make them pay?”&nbsp;

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:53.400
“Simple,” SCP-4494 answered. “The&nbsp;
price is they now have to face me.”&nbsp;

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:57.660
An hour later, the settlement was quiet.&nbsp;
The sharpshooter was still at his post,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:02.280
scanning the area nearby for signs of&nbsp;
movement. Sure enough, he spotted something:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:07.680
a group of figures approaching, the moonlight&nbsp;
glinting off their metallic outfits, revealing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:12.720
their positions as they drew closer and closer&nbsp;
to the makeshift town. The Slivers were coming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.520
but there would be something else waiting for&nbsp;
them when they made their way into the settlement.&nbsp;

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:23.280
The other settlers were awake, despite how late it&nbsp;
was, wearing their protective layers and peeking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.020
through cracked doors, only to slam them shut&nbsp;
as the glimmering gang crossed the threshold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:33.060
into their ramshackle home. The Slivers whooped&nbsp;
and jeered, brandishing weapons and threatening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:37.620
the settlers to show themselves, before the&nbsp;
bandits would break into their shacks and do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:42.540
to them what they’d done to their neighbors at the&nbsp;
other town. But as one of the Slivers approached&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:47.520
the door of a shack and began pounding his boot&nbsp;
against the metal door, something reached out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:54.180
the shadows and grabbed him. In fact, it wasn’t&nbsp;
coming from the shadows: it was the shadows.&nbsp;

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:59.280
Fists shrouded in darkness struck the remorseless&nbsp;
raider. Even with the protective layers covering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.560
his face, the Sliver could feel himself being&nbsp;
bruised by the beating. The Specter struck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.900
once more, knocking the wrongdoer unconscious and&nbsp;
wrenching the reflective metals from his outfit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:16.140
shattering them underfoot. The other Slivers&nbsp;
panicked, one drawing a handgun and firing. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:21.000
shots were useless, all they did was illuminate&nbsp;
the silhouette of a dark-cloaked figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.740
walking closer and closer, ready to&nbsp;
make them suffer for their crimes.&nbsp;

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:31.380
It was dusk by the time The Specter had beaten&nbsp;
the group of bandits, stripping them of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:36.120
distinctive reflective pieces. Each one of&nbsp;
the Slivers had been beaten into submission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:41.160
suffering broken ribs, black eyes, and&nbsp;
missing teeth. With the danger over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:46.260
the sharpshooter and the other settlers had&nbsp;
emerged from their hiding places, all eager&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:51.420
to weigh in on how best to punish the bandits.
Many yelled that they should be strung up without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:59.040
their protective gear, so that the sun melted them&nbsp;
into an SCP-001-A. But The Specter interjected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:03.540
urging the settlers not to sink to the level&nbsp;
of the criminals they had been harassed by.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:09.780
Instead, he turned to the defeated Slivers.
“Turn over half of your food, water, and medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:17.940
supplies to these people,” SCP-4494 demanded in a&nbsp;
frighteningly calm voice. “Then leave. Walk into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:22.380
these wastes and don’t come back.”
The Slivers agreed and fled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:27.720
running as fast as they could away from the town.
“Why’d you let them go?” the sharpshooter asked.&nbsp;

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:34.320
“These are uncertain times,” The Specter replied,&nbsp;
noticing the Sun was creeping over the horizon;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:39.780
it’d be time for him to go soon. “In the face&nbsp;
of hardship, it can be easy to lose our way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:45.900
Justice has always been blind; not blinded&nbsp;
by the sunlight, but blind to prevent bias.”&nbsp;

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:49.440
“The Slivers might come back,&nbsp;
though,” the man said, adding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:55.260
“If they even survive with what you left ‘em.”
“Maybe they’ll live out there,” SCP-4494&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.260 --> 00:12:03.300
responded. “Then again, perhaps not. But they have&nbsp;
a chance. That is justice, in a time without law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:07.200
it is the best we can offer.”
“And if they carry on raiding folks?”&nbsp;

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:12.780
“If they harm others, if they want to waste&nbsp;
the chance they’ve been given, then that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:20.220
their choice. But they know, if they refuse to&nbsp;
change, then they will answer to The Specter.”&nbsp;

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:25.320
With that, the shadowy crimefighter walked away&nbsp;
from the settlement. The unforgiving light of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:30.960
the Sun made him fade as he sauntered off like&nbsp;
an old gunslinger. But he’d be back. As long as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:36.900
people needed saving, he’d always be back.
